        "original_id": "00a49e88-5ce1-50f0-9852-0e8d2e06ddce",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lynyrd Skynyrd band members, backup singer\n- Organizations: Lynyrd Skynyrd, L&J Company\n- Events: 1977 Convair CV-240 crash\n- Places: Gillsburg, Mississippi; Greenville, South Carolina; Baton Rouge, Louisiana; Addison, Texas\n\nFacts:\n- On October 20, 1977, a Convair CV-240 chartered by Lynyrd Skynyrd from L&J Company of Addison, Texas, ran out of fuel and crashed in Gillsburg, Mississippi.\n- The Convair CV-240 crash occurred near the end of a flight from Greenville, South Carolina, to Baton Rouge, Louisiana.\n- In 1977, at the peak of Lynyrd Skynyrd's success, two band members and a backup singer died in the airplane crash.\n- The 1977 airplane crash abruptly ended Lynyrd Skynyrd's most popular incarnation.",
